st - simple terminal
--------------------
st is a simple virtual terminal emulator for X which sucks less.

Modified to run on RS-97.
=> line doubling to deal with the 320x480 resolution
=> TTF fonts replaced by embedded pixel font (from TIC-80)
=> onscreen keyboard (see keyboard.c for button bindings)

Chinese / RetroFW D88
---------------------
UTF-8 Chinese output is supported with an external GNU Unifont bitmap.
On full physical keyboards, a help page is shown at startup; any key dismisses
it and F1 toggles it again. Tap Shift for an offline Pinyin candidate window;
Shift chords retain uppercase/symbol input. Selected Chinese is sent as UTF-8
to the PTY for shell, Vim and other terminal applications.
Run `make package-d8` to fetch the font, cross-compile with the RetroFW SDK,
and prepare .build/d88/ for copying to the handheld. See README.zh-CN.md for
deployment, font selection, encoding requirements and verification commands.

Keys: 
- pad: select key
- A: press key
- B: toggles key (useful for shift/ctrl...)
- L: is shift
- R: is backspace
- Y: change keyboard location (top/bottom)
- X: show / hide keyboard
- SELECT: quit


Requirements
------------
In order to build st you need the Xlib header files.


Installation
------------
Edit config.mk to match your local setup (st is installed into
the /usr/local namespace by default).

Afterwards enter the following command to build and install st (if
necessary as root):

    make clean install


Running st
----------
If you don't install st, define TNAME to "xterm" in config.h or make sure to at
least compile st terminfo entry with the following command:

    tic -s st.info

It should print the path of the compiled terminfo entry. You can
safely remove it if you don't plan to use st anymore.
See the man page for additional details.

